<title>UK: Aluminium output falls in March, without China - IPA.</title>
<headline>Aluminium output falls in March, without China - IPA.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-04-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>Daily average primary aluminium output in March fell to 52,800 tonnes compared with 57,000 in February and 50,600 in March 1996, provisional figures from the International Primary Aluminium Institute (IPAI) show.</p>
<p>Total production in March (31 days) was 1.636 million tonnes, compared with 1.596 million in February (28 days) and 1.570 million in March 1996.</p>
<p>The latest figures do not include data for China. However, the data for February still include the Chinese statistics. Also aggregate data for 1997 will still include figures for China.  </p>
<p>The regional breakdown of primary aluminium production was as follows (in thousands of tonnes) the IPAI said.</p>
<p>			Mar 97   Feb 97    Mar 96</p>
<p>Africa		    94     84	 76</p>
<p>N.America		504    455	 496</p>
<p>S.America		180    163	 179</p>
<p>East/South Asia	162    267	 138</p>
<p>Europe West	    274    247	 270</p>
<p>Europe East/Central  279    251	 273</p>
<p>Ocenaia		  143    129	 138</p>
